nodes.prompt:
Write one image prompt per scene for e-commerce product photography. Use at most the first 4 scenes listed; ignore any beyond that.

Scenes: {{inputs.scenes}}
Brand style: {{inputs.style}}

Product notes:
{{prep.output}}

Rules for each prompt (max 70 words): keep the product exactly as described (same shape, colors, label, proportions), make it the clear hero and fully in frame; be concrete about surface, props, composition, lighting and lens. White background = pure seamless #FFFFFF studio sweep, soft even light, subtle contact shadow, no props. Lifestyle = realistic in-use setting that fits the product's buyer, shallow depth of field. Flat lay = top-down overhead on a styled surface with a few complementary props. No added text, logos or watermarks.

Output only lines in this format, one per scene:
<scene-slug>: <prompt>
where scene-slug is lowercase-with-dashes (e.g. white-background).

Write a short Markdown file to "$ARTIFACTS_DIR/README.md" (do not call any image API). Include: a title "Product photo studio", the product input (one line), whether the background was removed, then a table with columns File, Scene, Model, Prompt listing every image saved in $ARTIFACTS_DIR (the source image and cutout.png too, if present). Add one line of listing tips (e.g. use the white-background shot as the main image). Reply with the README path.

Product input:
{{inputs.product}}

Prep notes:
{{prep.output}}

Render results:
{{render.output}}
